pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% THE OPPOSITE-VERDICT COMPANION, same formula and same binary: what the formula actually
% is. Its three solutions over the preserved set {x1,x2} have objective 1, 1 and 2, so the
% optimum is 1 — and `soli` may install the objective-restricting constraint that proves it,
% because `conclusion BOUNDS` is a claim about the objective and not about the solution set.
% What the forgery does with the same constraint is EXPORT it as an equienumerable output.
f 1 ;
soli x1 ~x2 : 1 ;
rup >= 1 ;
output NONE ;
conclusion BOUNDS 1 1 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
